WEBVTT

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.595
has made the definition
seem bigger and blurrier.

00:05:02.619 --> 00:05:04.959
AHP: The way I think
of our contemporary burnout

00:05:04.983 --> 00:05:07.446
is you go until you feel
like you can't go anymore,

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.670
and then you keep going.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:13.456
So there's no catharsis,
there's no finishing the marathon.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.766
The feeling that everything
in your life flattens

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.246
into one long to-do list.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.466
And that means all of the joyful things,

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.336
all of the pain-in-the-butt things,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.416
like, they all just kind of become
one damn thing after another.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.488
AG: So I don't buy that this is burnout,

00:05:27.512 --> 00:05:28.996
because as a psychologist,

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.096
I've always thought about burnout
as emotional exhaustion,